.TH N-MAPPED 1 "" "n-mapped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
n-mapped \- beginner-friendly local GUI for Nmap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B n-mapped
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBn-mapped\fR launches a local HTTP server on \fI127.0.0.1\fR and opens a
browser-based UI that lets you click, search, and combine Nmap flags and NSE
scripts without memorizing CLI syntax. It drives the system \fBnmap\fR(1)
binary as a subprocess, parses its XML output, and persists scan history and
favorites under \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/n-mapped/\fR (Linux) or
\fI~/Library/Application\ Support/n-mapped/\fR (macOS).
.PP
The UI is embedded in the \fBn-mapped\fR binary at build time; no Node or
Python runtime is required at runtime. The only dependency is \fBnmap\fR
itself, version 7.40 or later.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-bind " \fIhost:port\fR"
Address the local HTTP server listens on. Default \fI127.0.0.1:8765\fR.
Refuses non-loopback addresses unless \fI\-\-allow-remote\fR is also set.
.TP
.BR \-\-nmap-path " \fIpath\fR"
Override the location of the \fBnmap\fR binary. Default: PATH lookup.
.TP
.BR \-\-privileged
Advisory flag indicating the user wants raw-socket scans enabled. Actual
elevation comes from running via \fIsudo\fR(1) or having \fIcap_net_raw\fR on
the binary; without those, this flag prints a warning.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-browser
Do not auto-open a browser tab on startup.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print the build version and exit.
.SH PRIVILEGE MODEL
TCP SYN, UDP, OS detection, and similar scans require raw sockets. The app
does not request privileges itself; instead, launch it elevated:
.PP
.RS 4
\fIsudo n-mapped\fR
.RE
.PP
Once elevated, the UI unlocks all flags. When unprivileged, the same flags
are visibly disabled with an explainer tooltip and the TCP Connect scan
(\-sT) is offered as a no-root alternative.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/n-mapped/history/<id>.json
Per-scan history records (Linux). Replace prefix with
\fI~/Library/Application\ Support/n-mapped/\fR on macOS.
.TP
.I .../n-mapped/favorites/<id>.json
Saved scan templates the user can re-apply.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
the Nmap Reference Guide at \fIhttps://nmap.org/book/\fR.
.SH BUGS
Report at \fIhttps://github.com/nick-the-descended/n-mapped/issues\fR.
